summary:
RESP (REdis Serialization Protocol) is the human-readable, high-speed binary-safe text protocol Redis uses over TCP: Simple Strings start with + (e.g. +OK
) • Errors start with - (e.g. -ERR unknown command
) • Integers start with : (e.g. :1000
).

Fixed-Size Chunking with Overlap: Splits text strictly by token count (e.g. 500 tokens with 50-token overlap) • Recursive Character Chunking: Recursively splits by paragraphs (

), then sentences (
), then words to preserve semantic structure.
